{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"R-31:25\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The answer that Allah created the heavens and earth is followed by قُلِ ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ, making praise a response to recognized creative lordship; بَلْ أَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ then exposes recognition that stops short of knowledge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"31:25\",\"ar\":\"مَّنْ خَلَقَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضَ لَيَقُولُنَّ ٱللَّهُ ۚ قُلِ ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ ۚ بَلْ أَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"Creator-confession, commanded praise, and the judgment about knowledge occur in one sequence.\",\"limits\":\"The verse does not specify what the questioners fail to know beyond its closing judgment.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-31:26\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The title ٱلْحَمِيدُ follows the statement that everything in the heavens and earth belongs to Allah, joining universal possession with the quality celebrated by ٱلْحَمْدُ in the focus.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"31:26\",\"ar\":\"لِلَّهِ مَا فِى ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ ۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ هُوَ ٱلْغَنِىُّ ٱلْحَمِيدُ\"}],\"activation\":\"The ownership claim immediately before ٱلْحَمِيدُ supplies the domain for this divine title.\",\"limits\":\"This verse uses an adjective meaning praised, while the focus states praise as a nominal clause.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-32:2\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The book is described as coming مِن رَّبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ, so the focus’s lordship title also identifies the source of revelation.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"32:2\",\"ar\":\"تَنزِيلُ ٱلْكِتَٰبِ لَا رَيْبَ فِيهِ مِن رَّبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The exact title رب العالمين is attached to the descent of the book.\",\"limits\":\"This occurrence establishes revelation’s source; it does not repeat the focus’s praise clause.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-32:15\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The believers who prostrate at reminders also وَسَبَّحُوا۟ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّهِمْ, giving the focus’s praise-and-lordship pairing an embodied devotional scene.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"32:15\",\"ar\":\"خَرُّوا۟ سُجَّدًۭا وَسَبَّحُوا۟ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّهِمْ وَهُمْ لَا يَسْتَكْبِرُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The scene joins remembrance of signs, prostration, glorification, and praise of their Lord.\",\"limits\":\"The verse depicts a response by believers, not the focus’s unrestricted nominal declaration.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-34:1\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"This opening joins praise to Allah’s possession of the heavens and earth, then explicitly places praise in the afterlife too; the focus’s universal praise thus has a stated final-life setting elsewhere in the Quran.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"34:1\",\"ar\":\"ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِى لَهُۥ مَا فِى ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَا فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ وَلَهُ ٱلْحَمْدُ فِى ٱلْءَاخِرَةِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The repeated praise clause extends from cosmic ownership into the afterlife.\",\"limits\":\"This verse names heavens and earth and the afterlife; it does not use the phrase العالمين.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-34:6\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The revealed truth guides to صِرَٰطِ ٱلْعَزِيزِ ٱلْحَمِيدِ, pairing the praised divine quality with guidance from the Lord who sent revelation.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"34:6\",\"ar\":\"مِن رَّبِّكَ هُوَ ٱلْحَقَّ وَيَهْدِىٓ إِلَىٰ صِرَٰطِ ٱلْعَزِيزِ ٱلْحَمِيدِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The verse names the Lord as revelation’s source and calls the guided path the path of the Praiseworthy.\",\"limits\":\"It does not state الحمد لله or رب العالمين as a formula.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-35:1\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Praise opens a description of Allah as فَاطِرِ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ, maker of angels, and one who increases creation as He wills; this grounds praise in origination and continuing creative scope.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"35:1\",\"ar\":\"ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ فَاطِرِ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ جَاعِلِ ٱلْمَلَٰٓئِكَةِ رُسُلًا\"},{\"ref\":\"35:1\",\"ar\":\"يَزِيدُ فِى ٱلْخَلْقِ مَا يَشَآءُ\"}],\"activation\":\"The appositional titles after ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ specify creative acts across the heavens, earth, and angelic order.\",\"limits\":\"This passage describes creation rather than using the focus’s title رب العالمين.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-35:34\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Garden dwellers say ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ because He removed their grief, and call Him غَفُورٌۭ شَكُورٌ; the formula can voice gratitude for a particular deliverance as well as unqualified praise.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"35:34\",\"ar\":\"وَقَالُوا۟ ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِىٓ أَذْهَبَ عَنَّا ٱلْحَزَنَ ۖ إِنَّ رَبَّنَا لَغَفُورٌۭ شَكُورٌ\"}],\"activation\":\"The speakers explain their praise through grief’s removal and address Allah as their Lord.\",\"limits\":\"This is a response by saved people to a specified gift, whereas the focus gives no occasion for praise.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-36:25\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The threatened speaker publicly says ءَامَنتُ بِرَبِّكُمْ, making belief in the Lord a spoken allegiance in a scene of opposition.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"36:25\",\"ar\":\"إِنِّىٓ ءَامَنتُ بِرَبِّكُمْ فَٱسْمَعُونِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The surrounding scene has just presented the speaker’s rejection of the audience’s error and his call to follow the messengers.\",\"limits\":\"The verse does not specify رب العالمين or connect this testimony directly to praise.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"low\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-37:4\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The declaration إِنَّ إِلَٰهَكُمْ لَوَٰحِدٌۭ is immediately expanded as lordship over the heavens, earth, what lies between them, and the easts; the adjacent sequence links the focus’s universal Lord title with exclusive deity.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"37:4\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ إِلَٰهَكُمْ لَوَٰحِدٌۭ\"},{\"ref\":\"37:5\",\"ar\":\"رَّبُّ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا وَرَبُّ ٱلْمَشَٰرِقِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The next ayah names cosmic domains under the one deity just affirmed.\",\"limits\":\"The sequence expands the title through specified cosmic regions rather than repeating العالمين.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-37:5\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"This passage spells out cosmic scope as the heavens, earth, what lies between, and the easts, giving concrete domains to the focus’s concise رب العالمين.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"37:5\",\"ar\":\"رَّبُّ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا وَرَبُّ ٱلْمَشَٰرِقِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The repeated رَبُّ governs a widening list of regions after the affirmation of divine oneness.\",\"limits\":\"The list does not claim to be a complete definition of العالمين.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-37:41\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The sincere servants have رِزْقٌۭ مَّعْلُومٌۭ, followed by fruit and honor, presenting provision as one concrete relation between Allah and His servants.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"37:40\",\"ar\":\"إِلَّا عِبَادَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلْمُخْلَصِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"37:41\",\"ar\":\"أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ رِزْقٌۭ مَّعْلُومٌۭ\"},{\"ref\":\"37:42\",\"ar\":\"فَوَٰكِهُ ۖ وَهُم مُّكْرَمُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The sequence specifies what the servants receive after identifying them as Allah’s sincere servants.\",\"limits\":\"It shows provision in a particular garden scene; it does not name the focus’s praise formula or title.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-37:79\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The salutation سَلَٰمٌ عَلَىٰ نُوحٍۢ فِى ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ uses the focus’s same noun in a scene of prophetic remembrance, bringing the inhabitants or communities among whom Noah is honored into the range of العالمين.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"37:79\",\"ar\":\"سَلَٰمٌ عَلَىٰ نُوحٍۢ فِى ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The surah’s sequence of messenger stories culminates in peace upon Noah among العالمين.\",\"limits\":\"This phrase does not settle whether العالمين in 1:2 means communities, created realms, or encompasses both.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-37:87\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Abraham asks what his audience thinks of رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ directly after challenging their desire for gods besides Allah; the focus’s title carries an anti-idol implication in this scene.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"37:86\",\"ar\":\"أَئِفْكًا ءَالِهَةًۭ دُونَ ٱللَّهِ تُرِيدُونَ\"},{\"ref\":\"37:87\",\"ar\":\"فَمَا ظَنُّكُم بِرَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The question about the Lord of all worlds follows an explicit challenge to worship of other gods.\",\"limits\":\"Abraham’s question does not repeat the focus’s الحمد clause.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-37:149\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-37:164\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-37:182\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The surah ends وَٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ after its closing salutation to the messengers, making the focus’s exact formula a fitting conclusion to a sequence of prophetic stories and divine judgments.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"37:181\",\"ar\":\"وَسَلَٰمٌ عَلَى ٱلْمُرْسَلِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"37:182\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The exact formula closes the surah immediately after peace upon the messengers.\",\"limits\":\"The later occurrence confirms a closing use; it does not establish that 1:2 itself is a surah ending.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-38:61\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-38:66\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The Lord is named as رَبُّ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا and paired with might and forgiveness, concretely expanding cosmic lordship beyond the focus’s compact title.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"38:66\",\"ar\":\"رَبُّ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا ٱلْعَزِيزُ ٱلْغَفَّٰرُ\"}],\"activation\":\"The surrounding declaration of divine oneness leads into this description of the Lord’s domain and attributes.\",\"limits\":\"This verse does not include the focus’s praise wording.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-38:79\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"Even Iblis addresses Allah as رَبِّ while asking for respite, placing his request under the authority he has defied.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"38:78\",\"ar\":\"وَإِنَّ عَلَيْكَ لَعْنَتِىٓ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ ٱلدِّينِ\"},{\"ref\":\"38:79\",\"ar\":\"قَالَ رَبِّ فَأَنظِرْنِىٓ إِلَىٰ يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The dialogue has just assigned Iblis a curse lasting to the Day of Judgment.\",\"limits\":\"The address shares the title Rabb but gives no universal domain or praise formula.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-39:29\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"After contrasting a man shared among quarrelsome masters with one devoted to one master, the verse says ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ; the focus’s praise is thus heard beside an argument for unentangled sovereignty.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"39:29\",\"ar\":\"رَّجُلًۭا فِيهِ شُرَكَآءُ مُتَشَٰكِسُونَ وَرَجُلًۭا سَلَمًۭا لِّرَجُلٍ هَلْ يَسْتَوِيَانِ مَثَلًا ۚ ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The praise formula follows a parable about divided service and exclusive belonging.\",\"limits\":\"The parable concerns a human master relationship; it does not define every sense of divine lordship.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-39:31\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The disputing parties are gathered عِندَ رَبِّكُمْ on the Day of Resurrection, placing the focus’s universal Lordship in a final scene where all parties answer before their Lord.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"39:31\",\"ar\":\"ثُمَّ إِنَّكُمْ يَوْمَ ٱلْقِيَٰمَةِ عِندَ رَبِّكُمْ تَخْتَصِمُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The verse makes the Lord the setting for the dispute that follows death.\",\"limits\":\"It does not identify the parties’ dispute or repeat الحمد لله رب العالمين.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-39:69\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"At the judgment scene, the earth shines بِنُورِ رَبِّهَا, presenting the earthly domain under its Lord as judgment is carried out.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"39:69\",\"ar\":\"وَأَشْرَقَتِ ٱلْأَرْضُ بِنُورِ رَبِّهَا وَوُضِعَ ٱلْكِتَٰبُ\"}],\"activation\":\"The earth’s illumination occurs alongside the placing of the record and judgment among people.\",\"limits\":\"The verse describes the earth in this scene and does not name all worlds or state a praise response.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-39:74\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The saved say ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ because Allah fulfilled His promise and granted them the earth; the next verse widens their thanks into the angels’ praise and the focus’s exact universal formula.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"39:74\",\"ar\":\"وَقَالُوا۟ ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِى صَدَقَنَا وَعْدَهُۥ وَأَوْرَثَنَا ٱلْأَرْضَ\"},{\"ref\":\"39:75\",\"ar\":\"يُسَبِّحُونَ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّهِمْ ۖ وَقُضِىَ بَيْنَهُم بِٱلْحَقِّ وَقِيلَ ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The adjacent verses move from the saved community’s specific thanks to praise surrounding the Throne after judgment.\",\"limits\":\"The speakers in 39:74 name fulfilled promise and inheritance; the focus does not specify an occasion.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-39:75\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Angels surround the Throne praising their Lord as judgment is completed, and the scene closes with the focus’s exact formula; its praise becomes the final utterance after justice is done.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"39:75\",\"ar\":\"وَتَرَى ٱلْمَلَٰٓئِكَةَ حَآفِّينَ مِنْ حَوْلِ ٱلْعَرْشِ يُسَبِّحُونَ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّهِمْ ۖ وَقُضِىَ بَيْنَهُم بِٱلْحَقِّ وَقِيلَ ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The exact phrase follows the account of angels’ praise and judgment completed with justice.\",\"limits\":\"This is a final judgment scene; the focus itself does not specify this setting.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-40:65\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"After calling people to invoke Allah with sincere devotion, the verse states the focus’s exact praise formula, then commands submission to the Lord of the worlds; praise sits within an explicit sequence of exclusive worship.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"40:65\",\"ar\":\"فَٱدْعُوهُ مُخْلِصِينَ لَهُ ٱلدِّينَ ۗ ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"40:66\",\"ar\":\"وَأُمِرْتُ أَنْ أُسْلِمَ لِرَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"Invocation, praise, and submission to رب العالمين occur in consecutive verses.\",\"limits\":\"This sequence is an exhortation; 1:2 is a declaration without an explicit command to worship.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-41:9\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"After confronting those who disbelieve in the Creator and assign Him rivals, the verse concludes ذَٰلِكَ رَبُّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ; lordship of all worlds is directly grounded in creation and set against rival-making.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"41:9\",\"ar\":\"قُلْ أَئِنَّكُمْ لَتَكْفُرُونَ بِٱلَّذِى خَلَقَ ٱلْأَرْضَ فِى يَوْمَيْنِ وَتَجْعَلُونَ لَهُۥٓ أَندَادًۭا ۚ ذَٰلِكَ رَبُّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The verse identifies the earth’s Creator as Lord of the worlds after challenging disbelief and the making of rivals.\",\"limits\":\"The immediate creation claim concerns earth; the title itself extends beyond that one act.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-43:14\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Travelers acknowledge that they will return to their Lord, while the next verse calls assigning Him a share from His servants clear ingratitude; the sequence sets acknowledgment of return against a false attribution to Allah.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"43:13\",\"ar\":\"سُبْحَٰنَ ٱلَّذِى سَخَّرَ لَنَا هَٰذَا وَمَا كُنَّا لَهُۥ مُقْرِنِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"43:14\",\"ar\":\"وَإِنَّآ إِلَىٰ رَبِّنَا لَمُنقَلِبُونَ\"},{\"ref\":\"43:15\",\"ar\":\"وَجَعَلُوا۟ لَهُۥ مِنْ عِبَادِهِۦ جُزْءًا ۚ إِنَّ ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ لَكَفُورٌۭ مُّبِينٌ\"}],\"activation\":\"The travel prayer names Allah’s control and the travelers’ return; the next ayah condemns an attribution made to Him.\",\"limits\":\"The focus does not state the return-to-Allah motif or the specific false attribution in this passage.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-43:46\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Moses identifies himself as a messenger of رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ, and the audience responds to his signs with mockery; the focus’s universal title appears in a mission whose authority is actively contested.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"43:46\",\"ar\":\"فَقَالَ إِنِّى رَسُولُ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"43:47\",\"ar\":\"فَلَمَّا جَآءَهُم بِـَٔايَٰتِنَآ إِذَا هُم مِّنْهَا يَضْحَكُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The exact title is Moses’ message to Firawn and his assembly, immediately followed by their reaction.\",\"limits\":\"Their mockery does not show that they understood or accepted the title.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-44:20\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"Moses seeks refuge بِرَبِّى وَرَبِّكُمْ while addressing the people threatening him, presenting the Lord as protector of both sides of the confrontation.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"44:20\",\"ar\":\"وَإِنِّى عُذْتُ بِرَبِّى وَرَبِّكُمْ أَن تَرْجُمُونِ\"}],\"activation\":\"Moses names a shared Lord as he asks his audience not to stone him.\",\"limits\":\"The verse does not specify رب العالمين or describe the outcome of the appeal.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-45:36\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"After the account of those who cannot leave the Fire, the surah declares praise to the Lord of the heavens, earth, and worlds; praise is voiced alongside an assertion of cosmic sovereignty after judgment.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"45:35\",\"ar\":\"فَٱلْيَوْمَ لَا يُخْرَجُونَ مِنْهَا وَلَا هُمْ يُسْتَعْتَبُونَ\"},{\"ref\":\"45:36\",\"ar\":\"فَلِلَّهِ ٱلْحَمْدُ رَبِّ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَرَبِّ ٱلْأَرْضِ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The praise formula follows the judgment scene and expands its Lord title across heavens, earth, and all worlds.\",\"limits\":\"The passage does not say that those punished are the speakers of praise.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-46:25\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The destructive wind acts بِأَمْرِ رَبِّهَا, showing a natural force as an agent operating by its Lord’s command; the focus’s title can be heard against this concrete instance of governance.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"46:25\",\"ar\":\"تُدَمِّرُ كُلَّ شَىْءٍۭ بِأَمْرِ رَبِّهَا فَأَصْبَحُوا۟ لَا يُرَىٰٓ إِلَّا مَسَٰكِنُهُمْ\"}],\"activation\":\"The wind’s destruction and the remnant of dwellings are explicitly tied to its Lord’s command.\",\"limits\":\"The verse does not use the phrase رب العالمين or identify the wind as one of the meanings of العالمين.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-50:4\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-51:34\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-51:44\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-52:37\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The rhetorical questions about the Lord’s خزائن and whether the audience are المُصَيْطِرُونَ place possession and control in view, concrete aspects of the focus’s title ربّ.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"52:37\",\"ar\":\"أَمْ عِندَهُمْ خَزَآئِنُ رَبِّكَ أَمْ هُمُ ٱلْمُصَۣيْطِرُونَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The passage challenges the audience’s claims to stores and control by asking whether these belong to them.\",\"limits\":\"It does not repeat the focus’s title or specify what the Lord’s خزائن contain.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-52:48\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The command to be patient لِحُكْمِ رَبِّكَ is paired with وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ, connecting praise to steadfastness under judgment and pressure.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"52:48\",\"ar\":\"وَٱصْبِرْ لِحُكْمِ رَبِّكَ فَإِنَّكَ بِأَعْيُنِنَا ۖ وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ حِينَ تَقُومُ\"}],\"activation\":\"Patience for the Lord’s judgment and glorification with His praise are joined in one address.\",\"limits\":\"The verse is an instruction to the Prophet and does not state the focus’s nominal clause.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-53:5\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-53:42\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The verse names the Lord as the final destination, إِلَىٰ رَبِّكَ ٱلْمُنتَهَىٰ; lordship here includes the endpoint toward which all things return.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"53:42\",\"ar\":\"وَأَنَّ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكَ ٱلْمُنتَهَىٰ\"}],\"activation\":\"The statement follows the account of each person receiving full recompense for their effort.\",\"limits\":\"It specifies an endpoint but does not give a description of the return’s manner.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-53:49\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Allah is called رَبُّ ٱلشِّعْرَىٰ, explicitly Lord of Sirius; the focus’s رب العالمين can encompass even a named star that receives a specific Lord-title here.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"53:49\",\"ar\":\"وَأَنَّهُۥ هُوَ رَبُّ ٱلشِّعْرَىٰ\"}],\"activation\":\"The ayah assigns Lordship over Sirius to Allah in a sequence naming divine acts and the fates of earlier peoples.\",\"limits\":\"This occurrence names one celestial object and does not explain why Sirius is singled out.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-55:17\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The Lord is described as رَبُّ ٱلْمَشْرِقَيْنِ وَرَبُّ ٱلْمَغْرِبَيْنِ, giving the focus’s broad title a paired horizon setting.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"55:17\",\"ar\":\"رَبُّ ٱلْمَشْرِقَيْنِ وَرَبُّ ٱلْمَغْرِبَيْنِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The paired east and west titles interrupt the surah’s refrain asking which favors the two audiences deny.\",\"limits\":\"The verse does not identify the two easts and two wests or equate them directly with العالمين.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-55:27\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"After declaring that all on earth pass away, the surah says وَيَبْقَىٰ وَجْهُ رَبِّكَ, setting the persistence of the Lord against the transience of creation.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"55:26\",\"ar\":\"كُلُّ مَنْ عَلَيْهَا فَانٍۢ\"},{\"ref\":\"55:27\",\"ar\":\"وَيَبْقَىٰ وَجْهُ رَبِّكَ ذُو ٱلْجَلَٰلِ وَٱلْإِكْرَامِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The persistence clause directly follows the statement that all upon the earth are passing away.\",\"limits\":\"This passage describes the Lord’s face and persistence, not the duration or fate of every world.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-55:32\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The question فَبِأَىِّ ءَالَآءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبَانِ addresses both jinn and humans after their challenge to pass beyond the bounds of heavens and earth, linking denial of favor with creaturely limits.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"55:31\",\"ar\":\"سَنَفْرُغُ لَكُمْ أَيُّهَ ٱلثَّقَلَانِ\"},{\"ref\":\"55:32\",\"ar\":\"فَبِأَىِّ ءَالَآءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبَانِ\"},{\"ref\":\"55:33\",\"ar\":\"يَٰمَعْشَرَ ٱلْجِنِّ وَٱلْإِنسِ إِنِ ٱسْتَطَعْتُمْ أَن تَنفُذُوا۟ مِنْ أَقْطَارِ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ فَٱنفُذُوا۟\"}],\"activation\":\"The paired pronoun in the refrain addresses both groups immediately before their attempted escape is challenged.\",\"limits\":\"The passage does not use الحمد or رب العالمين; the link is through the Lord’s favors and the addressed creation.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-55:34\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The repeated question about the two groups’ favors comes after the warning of fire and molten copper, retaining the language of favor even as the passage announces punishment.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"55:33\",\"ar\":\"لَا تَنفُذُونَ إِلَّا بِسُلْطَٰنٍۢ\"},{\"ref\":\"55:34\",\"ar\":\"فَبِأَىِّ ءَالَآءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبَانِ\"},{\"ref\":\"55:35\",\"ar\":\"يُرْسَلُ عَلَيْكُمَا شُوَاظٌۭ مِّن نَّارٍۢ وَنُحَاسٌۭ فَلَا تَنتَصِرَانِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The refrain brackets the impossibility of escape and the coming punishment.\",\"limits\":\"The refrain’s question does not itself explain how punishment relates to divine favors.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-55:46\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"Fear of the Lord’s station is followed by two gardens, placing the focus’s Lord title in a frame of accountability and reward.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"55:46\",\"ar\":\"وَلِمَنْ خَافَ مَقَامَ رَبِّهِۦ جَنَّتَانِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The promise of gardens is grammatically attached to fear of the Lord’s station.\",\"limits\":\"This verse describes a reward for a particular response; it does not state the focus’s praise formula.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-55:78\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The surah closes with تَبَٰرَكَ ٱسْمُ رَبِّكَ ذِى ٱلْجَلَٰلِ وَٱلْإِكْرَامِ, a concluding benediction that joins the Lord’s name with majesty and generosity after the surah’s repeated account of favors.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"55:77\",\"ar\":\"فَبِأَىِّ ءَالَآءِ رَبِّكُمَا تُكَذِّبَانِ\"},{\"ref\":\"55:78\",\"ar\":\"تَبَٰرَكَ ٱسْمُ رَبِّكَ ذِى ٱلْجَلَٰلِ وَٱلْإِكْرَامِ\"}],\"activation\":\"This blessing of the Lord’s name concludes the surah’s refrain sequence.\",\"limits\":\"It names divine majesty and generosity rather than repeating الحمد لله رب العالمين.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-56:74\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"After describing fire as a reminder and provision, the verse commands فَسَبِّحْ بِٱسْمِ رَبِّكَ ٱلْعَظِيمِ, offering glorification as a response to signs of dependence.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"56:73\",\"ar\":\"نَحْنُ جَعَلْنَٰهَا تَذْكِرَةًۭ وَمَتَٰعًۭا لِّلْمُقْوِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"56:74\",\"ar\":\"فَسَبِّحْ بِٱسْمِ رَبِّكَ ٱلْعَظِيمِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The imperative follows the account of fire’s function as reminder and provision.\",\"limits\":\"The command uses tasbih, not the focus’s word الحمد.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-56:80\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The revelation is called تَنزِيلٌۭ مِّن رَّبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ, repeating the focus’s title to identify the source of scripture.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"56:80\",\"ar\":\"تَنزِيلٌۭ مِّن رَّبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The exact title qualifies the revelation in a passage defending its truth and origin.\",\"limits\":\"This verse states revelation’s source rather than a praise response.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-64:1\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Everything in the heavens and earth glorifies Allah, and the verse declares both dominion and praise His; the focus’s praise can be heard as the human utterance within a universal chorus of praise.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"64:1\",\"ar\":\"يُسَبِّحُ لِلَّهِ مَا فِى ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَا فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ ۖ لَهُ ٱلْمُلْكُ وَلَهُ ٱلْحَمْدُ\"}],\"activation\":\"The verse explicitly joins all creation’s glorification, Allah’s dominion, and praise belonging to Him.\",\"limits\":\"It does not use رب العالمين or specify how the creation’s glorification occurs.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-64:4\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The sequence from creating the heavens and earth to knowing what they contain and what people conceal could let the focus’s العالمين be heard as domains under both creative rule and knowledge, including hidden human interiors.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"64:3\",\"ar\":\"خَلَقَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضَ بِٱلْحَقِّ\"},{\"ref\":\"64:4\",\"ar\":\"يَعْلَمُ مَا فِى ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا تُسِرُّونَ وَمَا تُعْلِنُونَ\"}],\"missing\":\"A lexical or textual link showing that العالمين in 1:2 includes these domains of hidden knowledge is missing; another عالمين occurrence joined to knowledge or signs could clarify the connection.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-68:2\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-68:9\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-68:52\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The Quran is described as ذِكْرٌۭ لِّلْعَٰلَمِينَ, using the focus’s same noun for those to whom a reminder is addressed; the Lord of all worlds is thus paired elsewhere with a message directed to the alamin.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"68:52\",\"ar\":\"وَمَا هُوَ إِلَّا ذِكْرٌۭ لِّلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The phrase assigns a universal audience to the reminder.\",\"limits\":\"This occurrence does not identify precisely who is included in العالمين.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-69:43\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Revelation is again called تَنزِيلٌۭ مِّن رَّبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ, tying the focus’s Lord title to the source claim defended in this surah.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"69:42\",\"ar\":\"وَلَا بِقَوْلِ كَاهِنٍۢ ۚ قَلِيلًۭا مَّا تَذَكَّرُونَ\"},{\"ref\":\"69:43\",\"ar\":\"تَنزِيلٌۭ مِّن رَّبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"69:44\",\"ar\":\"وَلَوْ تَقَوَّلَ عَلَيْنَا بَعْضَ ٱلْأَقَاوِيلِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The source formula sits between denial that the message is a soothsayer’s speech and a warning against fabricating words about Allah.\",\"limits\":\"This passage argues for the Quran’s source; it does not repeat الحمد لله.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-69:52\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"After affirming the message as true certainty, the Prophet is commanded to glorify by the name of his عظِيم Lord, making glorification the response to revelation’s confirmation.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"69:51\",\"ar\":\"وَإِنَّهُۥ لَحَقُّ ٱلْيَقِينِ\"},{\"ref\":\"69:52\",\"ar\":\"فَسَبِّحْ بِٱسْمِ رَبِّكَ ٱلْعَظِيمِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The tasbih imperative follows the assertion of certainty.\",\"limits\":\"The verse commands glorification and does not state the focus’s praise formula.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-70:3\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-71:28\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"Noah’s closing prayer addresses his Lord on behalf of himself, his parents, believers entering his house, and believing men and women, making a particular community the object of supplication to Rabb.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"71:28\",\"ar\":\"رَّبِّ ٱغْفِرْ لِى وَلِوَٰلِدَىَّ وَلِمَن دَخَلَ بَيْتِىَ مُؤْمِنًۭا وَلِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَٱلْمُؤْمِنَٰتِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The vocative رَبِّ opens a prayer that names several groups for forgiveness.\",\"limits\":\"This is a specific petition, not praise of Allah as Lord of all worlds.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-73:9\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The Lord of east and west is declared the sole deity, followed by the command to take Him as guardian; the focus’s universal Lordship stands beside explicit exclusivity and reliance.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"73:9\",\"ar\":\"رَّبُّ ٱلْمَشْرِقِ وَٱلْمَغْرِبِ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ فَٱتَّخِذْهُ وَكِيلًۭا\"}],\"activation\":\"The verse joins cosmic extent, exclusive divinity, and personal reliance in one sequence.\",\"limits\":\"It names east and west rather than using العالمين and does not state a praise clause.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-74:3\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The command وَرَبَّكَ فَكَبِّرْ makes magnifying the Lord an early instruction in the surah’s program of warning and purification.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"74:2\",\"ar\":\"قُمْ فَأَنذِرْ\"},{\"ref\":\"74:3\",\"ar\":\"وَرَبَّكَ فَكَبِّرْ\"}],\"activation\":\"Magnification of the Lord follows the command to rise and warn.\",\"limits\":\"The verse commands takbir; it does not repeat the focus’s hamd wording.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-74:7\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-74:31\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The number and nature of the Lord’s forces are known to Allah alone, placing the focus’s Lordship alongside a stated limit on human knowledge of His armies.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"74:31\",\"ar\":\"وَمَا يَعْلَمُ جُنُودَ رَبِّكَ إِلَّا هُوَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The verse contrasts disputes over the number of Hell’s keepers with what only the Lord knows.\",\"limits\":\"It concerns the Lord’s armies in this passage and does not itself expand the referent of العالمين.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-75:30\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"On that day, the journey ends إِلَىٰ رَبِّكَ, giving the Lord title a personal destination within the resurrection scene.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"75:30\",\"ar\":\"إِلَىٰ رَبِّكَ يَوْمَئِذٍ ٱلْمَسَاقُ\"}],\"activation\":\"The verse follows the description of death’s bodily signs and names the direction of the final conveyance.\",\"limits\":\"It specifies the destination without describing the judgment that follows.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-78:4\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-78:36\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The reward is عَطَآءً حِسَابًۭا from “your Lord,” immediately identified as Lord of the heavens, earth, and what lies between; the passage joins a measured gift to cosmic lordship.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"78:36\",\"ar\":\"جَزَآءًۭ مِّن رَّبِّكَ عَطَآءً حِسَابًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"78:37\",\"ar\":\"رَّبِّ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The Lord who grants recompense is expanded in the next verse through the cosmic domain He rules.\",\"limits\":\"The gift belongs to the people described in the preceding passage, not an undifferentiated account of all creation.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"X1\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The Fatiha moves from بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ with the names ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ to ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ; the divine name invoked at the opening becomes the recipient of praise, and the praise is grounded in lordship over all worlds.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:1\",\"ar\":\"بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:2\",\"ar\":\"ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The repeated name Allah links the opening invocation to the next ayah’s praise and title.\",\"limits\":\"The sequence connects the clauses but does not state that praise is caused by the names of mercy.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}"}}
